// Approach: TreeSet — add every element from both arrays, then copy out.
//           The set handles duplicates and ordering automatically.
// Time: O((n+m) log(n+m)), Space: O(n+m)
// Note: first attempt used list.contains() inside the loop — that's an O(n)
//       scan per element, making the whole thing O(n²). A set's add() is
//       O(log n) for TreeSet, O(1) for HashSet (but unordered).
// Better solution exists: two pointers walking both sorted arrays together
